-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the bridge from codes (unverified)
-- a code of the fragment — applications of the globals plus and times, variables, Nat literals
-- as constructor codes — read as an expression; a code outside the fragment reads as none. What
-- it produces is decided by norm and the theorem is ring-eq about the typed expression, so the
-- bridge is the unverified part (18.13: search is unverified, the checker verified)
-- a Nat literal's code within k levels (a literal's code is a list field inside a code, which
-- structural recursion does not follow; the word eliminator recurses one level per step, so a
-- code is read as deep as it is, up to 2^64 levels, past which it reads as outside the fragment)
nat-of-code-k : Word → Code → Opt Nat
nat-of-code-k k =
  %welimP (λ v → Code → Opt Nat) k (λ c → none)
    (λ j h c → case c of
                 ccon d i fs ds → (if weq i #0 then some zero
                                   else (case fs of lcons n r → (case h n of none → none; some m → some (suc m)); _ → none))
                 _ → none)
